change:
  id: CHG-014
  title: Enforce the declared mutation contract in the scorer
  status: proposed
  intent: Give the deterministic scorer the accepted MutationContract and a typed evidence channel keyed by its declared required_evidence ids, so declared hard gates are enforced rather than described.
  audience_level: developer
  relates_to:
    - RISK-002
    - ARCH-001
    - CON-002
    - SYS-001

deltas:
  - op: ADDED
    capability: contract-aware-fitness
    requirement: The scorer receives the accepted contract and decides against what that contract declared, never against a fixed assumption about it.
    scenarios:
      - id: S1
        when: a contract declares a required_evidence id and the candidate produces no observed result for it
        then: the candidate is discarded on a hard gate naming the missing evidence id
        and:
          - the discard reason identifies the declared id rather than a generic failure
      - id: S2
        when: a contract declares a required_evidence id and an observed result for it reports failure
        then: the candidate is discarded on a hard gate naming that id
      - id: S3
        when: every declared required_evidence id has a passing observed result
        then: the declared gate contributes no discard and scoring proceeds to the weighted objectives
      - id: S4
        when: an observed evidence result is supplied for an id the contract did not declare
        then: it is recorded in the audit record and cannot satisfy or weaken any declared gate
        and:
          - undeclared evidence never substitutes for a declared id
      - id: S5
        when: the contract's operator declares an objective set different from the shared defaults
        then: the scorer gates and weights against the contract's own objectives
        and:
          - a weighted score is never computed against an objective set the contract did not declare
      - id: S6
        when: a caller scores without supplying a contract
        then: the existing fixed-gate behaviour is preserved for that call
        and:
          - the transitional entry point remains available until every caller supplies a contract

acceptance:
  - scenario: S1
    test_id: deterministic/ContractAwareFitnessTest.discardsWhenADeclaredEvidenceIdHasNoObservedResult
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S2
    test_id: deterministic/ContractAwareFitnessTest.discardsWhenADeclaredEvidenceIdReportsFailure
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S3
    test_id: deterministic/ContractAwareFitnessTest.proceedsToObjectivesWhenEveryDeclaredEvidenceIdPasses
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S4
    test_id: deterministic/ContractAwareFitnessTest.undeclaredEvidenceCannotSatisfyADeclaredGate
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S5
    test_id: deterministic/ContractAwareFitnessTest.weightsAgainstTheContractsOwnObjectiveSet
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S6
    test_id: deterministic/PhenotypeFitnessScorerTest.contractlessScoringPreservesTheExistingGates
    layer: unit

tasks:
  - id: T1
    slice: add a typed RequiredEvidenceResult keyed by declared evidence id, with a pass/fail outcome and a diagnostic
    status: pending
  - id: T2
    slice: add failing unit coverage for S1 through S5 against the new contract-aware entry point
    status: pending
  - id: T3
    slice: add the contract-aware scorer entry point and enforce declared required_evidence as a hard gate
    status: pending
  - id: T4
    slice: gate and weight against the contract's own objective set, and retire the everyOperatorSharesTheObjectiveSetTheScorerAssumes guard once it is no longer load-bearing
    status: pending
  - id: T5
    slice: thread the accepted contract from MutationEvaluationLoop through to the scorer
    status: pending
  - id: T6
    slice: record observed required-evidence results in the candidate audit record
    status: pending
  - id: T7
    slice: update RISK-002, CHG-002 T4b, README and wiki; close RISK-002 or record what remains
    status: pending

non_goals:
  - making behavioral_safety variable, which depends on this change and follows it
  - wiring the benchmarks module so cost_latency_budget has an evidence source
  - evaluating or ranking several candidates per generation
  - letting any model-produced judgement reach a score, a gate or a promotion decision
  - changing the promotion threshold or the default objective weights

risks:
  - the transitional contractless entry point keeps the old fixed-gate behaviour reachable, so a caller that is never migrated silently retains the weaker guarantee; T5 must migrate the live loop and T7 must record any caller left behind
  - enforcing declared evidence makes previously promotable candidates discard, which is the intended correction but will change recorded outcomes for any repeat of an earlier experiment
  - RISK-002 says promoted candidates still need human inspection until this lands; do not close that risk until the live loop actually supplies a contract
